│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the main failure mode: the model’s slope collapses out of sample        │
│                          │ because many current features are too slow and regime-specific. I’m making the feature    │
│                          │ set more regime-invariant by shifting from long-horizon absolute levels to shorter        │
│                          │ lookbacks, rolling z-scores, and rate-of-change style regime measures. I’m also           │
│                          │ tightening the XGBoost model to reduce overfitting to the train regime while keeping      │
│                          │ enough expressivity to preserve predictive slope.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Replace long lookbacks with shorter, more adaptive windows.                             │
│                          │ - Add rolling z-score normalization for returns, volatility, volume, and price position.  │
│                          │ - Add short-horizon regime-trend features such as volatility trend, efficiency trend, and │
│                          │ autocorrelation trend.                                                                    │
│                          │ - Add a simple momentum × volatility-regime interaction.                                  │
│                          │ - Slightly regularize the booster and reduce tree count to favor robust patterns.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should help raise validation slope and correlation while reducing train→val          │
│                          │ collapse, without increasing feature count beyond the limit.                              │
