│ patch_description        │ This edit attacks the main failure mode: the model’s slope collapses out-of-sample        │
│                          │ because the current feature set is dominated by longer-horizon, regime-specific levels.   │
│                          │ I’m shifting the feature space toward shorter, more adaptive windows and adding rolling   │
│                          │ z-score normalization so signals are expressed relative to their recent local regime      │
│                          │ rather than absolute price/volatility levels.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Concretely:                                                                               │
│                          │ - Reduce reliance on 20/60-bar horizons and add 5/10/15/20-bar momentum, volatility, and  │
│                          │ efficiency features.                                                                      │
│                          │ - Add rolling normalized versions of key momentum, volatility, ATR, RSI, MACD, and volume │
│                          │ features.                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Add rate-of-change regime features such as volatility trend and efficiency trend.       │
│                          │ - Keep the feature count under 80 while increasing regime robustness.                     │
│                          │ - Make the model slightly more conservative with stronger regularization and fewer trees  │
│                          │ to reduce memorization of the training regime.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should improve val slope and pred_std_ratio by making the learned relationships more │
│                          │ stationary across the train/test/val regime shifts.                                       │
